<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Hardened runtime entitlements for TheChatPlace.app (PyInstaller, onedir).

    Notarization requires the hardened runtime, which breaks CPython unless
    some exceptions are granted. The first four are Image Description
    Toolkit's proven set (BuildAndRelease/MacBuilds/entitlements.plist there);
    don't trim them without testing a notarized build on a Mac that has never
    run the app.

    allow-unsigned-executable-memory, allow-jit
        CPython and C extensions map writable-executable pages.
    disable-library-validation
        wxPython's and Python's libraries were built by others; they're
        re-signed here, but this keeps one that slips through loadable.
    allow-dyld-environment-variables
        The PyInstaller bootloader sets DYLD_* paths.
    automation.apple-events
        Speech through VoiceOver: speak-engine.sh asks VoiceOver to speak with
        osascript, an Apple Event that the hardened runtime blocks without
        this. macOS asks the user once (NSAppleEventsUsageDescription in
        Info.plist says why).

    Not sandboxed, so files, the network and running claude need nothing here.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
